IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), regulation 2 -- INTERPRETATION.
-- Piece cr1. LAYER 1: the law as the text states it; it takes nobody's point of view.
--
-- Regulation 2(1) defines "Act" and "Minister"; regulation 2(2) defines ten terms for the purposes of
-- "the Act and these Regulations" (so the Act's paragraph 6(2)(a), which says "agriculture", "fishing"
-- and so on, reads these words); regulation 2(3) defines "timber". The Act's piece (cp1) takes each of
-- these as a plain input; the rules below say how each is worked out from facts.
--
-- "Act" (line 13) is a pure citation and has no rule. The repealed entries (lines 14, 15 and 19) have none.
-- A definition that "means" a list is closed: an operation the list does not name is not that thing.
-- "agriculture" is the one definition that says "without limiting the generality of the foregoing", so
-- it alone answers NOTHING for an operation it does not name (fork F1 in NOTES.md).

§ `Regulations, regulation 2 -- interpretation`

§§ `Regulation 2(1): the Minister`

-- src:16 | Minister means
-- src:17 | (a) in Parts I, II, III and IV, the Minister of National Revenue, and
-- src:18 | (b) in Part V, the Minister as defined in subsection 42(1) of the Act. (ministre)
@ref Reg 2(1) "Minister" (src:16-18)
DECLARE `cr1 Part of the Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `the Regulations' Part I`
    `the Regulations' Part II`
    `the Regulations' Part III`
    `the Regulations' Part IV`
    `the Regulations' Part V`
    `the Regulations' Part VIII`

-- Minister means (a) in Parts I, II, III and IV, the Minister of National Revenue, and (b) in Part V,
-- the Minister as defined in subsection 42(1) of the Act (the Minister of Employment and Social
-- Development). The text defines the word for no other Part: Part VIII (regs 79 to 88) is left without
-- a definition, so the answer there is NOTHING (fork F2), not a guess.
@ref Reg 2(1) "Minister" (src:16-18)
GIVEN part IS A `cr1 Part of the Regulations`
GIVETH A MAYBE Minister
`reg 2(1) — the Minister in a Part of the Regulations` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `the Regulations' Part I` THEN JUST `the Minister of National Revenue`
    WHEN `the Regulations' Part II` THEN JUST `the Minister of National Revenue`
    WHEN `the Regulations' Part III` THEN JUST `the Minister of National Revenue`
    WHEN `the Regulations' Part IV` THEN JUST `the Minister of National Revenue`
    WHEN `the Regulations' Part V` THEN JUST `the Minister of Employment and Social Development`
    WHEN `the Regulations' Part VIII` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 2(2): the instruments the definitions apply to`

DECLARE `cr1 Instrument that uses a defined word` IS ONE OF
    `the Act`
    `these Regulations`
    `another instrument`

-- (2) For the purposes of the Act and these Regulations, ... The ten definitions of subsection (2) (and the
-- definition of timber in subsection (3), for the two definitions it serves) are the meaning of the words in
-- the Act, as well as in the Regulations. The Act's paragraph 6(2)(a) is the example.
-- src:20 | (2) For the purposes of the Act and these Regulations,
@ref Reg 2(2) chapeau (src:20)
GIVEN instrument IS A `cr1 Instrument that uses a defined word`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — the definitions of subsection (2) apply to an instrument` instrument MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `another instrument` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Regulation 2(2): agriculture and agricultural enterprise`

-- The operations the definition names. "the operations of farming" is the general core; (a) to (i) are
-- the listed operations; (j) and (k) are the two off-the-farm limbs.
-- src:21 | agriculture means the operations of farming when carried on on a farm for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer and, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, includes the operation of
-- src:22 | (a) the clearing of land for the purposes of farming,
-- src:23 | (b) the cultivation of the soil,
-- src:24 | (c) the conservation of the soil, including the construction, maintenance and operations of tile drainage systems, ditches, canals, reservoirs or waterways exclusively for the purposes of farming,
-- src:25 | (d) the producing, harvesting, storing or grading of any natural product of farming,
-- src:26 | (e) the preparation of land for or the harvesting of wild berries,
-- src:27 | (f) the raising of bees and producing of honey,
-- src:28 | (g) the breeding or raising of horses, beasts of burden, cattle, sheep, goats, swine, furbearing animals, birds of any kind or the production of eggs,
-- src:29 | (h) dairy farming and the processing of milk, butter or cheese on the farm where it is produced,
-- src:30 | (i) producing maple sap, maple syrup or maple sugar,
-- src:31 | when carried on on a farm for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer, and includes
-- src:32 | (j) the offering for sale or selling, off the farm for the benefit of such farmer, of any of the products of the operations previously described in this definition where such offering for sale or selling is incidental to those operations, and
-- src:33 | (k) the exhibiting, advertising, assembling, freezing, storing, grading, processing, packing and transporting, off the farm for the benefit of such farmer, of the products described in paragraph (j) where the exhibiting, advertising, assembling, freezing, storing, grading, processing, packing or transporting is incidental to the offering for sale or selling described in that paragraph; (agriculture)
@ref Reg 2(2) "agriculture" (src:21-33)
DECLARE `cr1 Operation in the definition of agriculture` IS ONE OF
    `the operations of farming`
    `the clearing of land for the purposes of farming`
    `the cultivation of the soil`
    `the conservation of the soil, including tile drainage systems, ditches, canals, reservoirs or waterways exclusively for farming`
    `the producing, harvesting, storing or grading of a natural product of farming`
    `the preparation of land for or the harvesting of wild berries`
    `the raising of bees and producing of honey`
    `the breeding or raising of horses, beasts of burden, cattle, sheep, goats, swine, furbearing animals or birds, or the production of eggs`
    `dairy farming and the processing of milk, butter or cheese on the farm where it is produced`
    `producing maple sap, maple syrup or maple sugar`
    `offering for sale or selling, off the farm, the products of the operations described`
    `exhibiting, advertising, assembling, freezing, storing, grading, processing, packing or transporting, off the farm, the products of that offering for sale or selling`
    `an operation that the definition does not name`

-- Operations in the general core and in (a) to (i) count when "carried on on a farm for the benefit of an
-- individual or other person who is a farmer". The two off-the-farm limbs (j) and (k) count when carried on
-- off the farm for the benefit of such a farmer and incidental to the operations (j) or the offering for
-- sale or selling (k) described. An operation the definition does not name is NOT decided (NOTHING).
@ref Reg 2(2) "agriculture" (src:21-33)
GIVEN operation IS A `cr1 Operation in the definition of agriculture`
      `carried on on a farm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `carried on for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `incidental to the operations or the offering for sale or selling described` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — an operation is agriculture` operation `carried on on a farm` `carried on for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer` `incidental to the operations or the offering for sale or selling described` MEANS
    CONSIDER operation
    WHEN `an operation that the definition does not name` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `offering for sale or selling, off the farm, the products of the operations described` THEN
        JUST (    (NOT `carried on on a farm`)
              AND `carried on for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer`
              AND `incidental to the operations or the offering for sale or selling described`)
    WHEN `exhibiting, advertising, assembling, freezing, storing, grading, processing, packing or transporting, off the farm, the products of that offering for sale or selling` THEN
        JUST (    (NOT `carried on on a farm`)
              AND `carried on for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer`
              AND `incidental to the operations or the offering for sale or selling described`)
    OTHERWISE
        JUST (    `carried on on a farm`
              AND `carried on for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer`)

-- src:34 | agricultural enterprise means the business of agriculture carried on for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer; (entreprise agricole)
@ref Reg 2(2) "agricultural enterprise" (src:34)
GIVEN `the business is the business of agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `carried on for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — a business is an agricultural enterprise` `the business is the business of agriculture` `carried on for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer` MEANS
    `the business is the business of agriculture` AND `carried on for the benefit of an individual or other person who is a farmer`

§§ `Regulation 2(2): fishing, hunting and trapping`

-- src:35 | fishing means fishing for or catching any fish, including shellfish, crustaceans or molluscs, or any aquatic animal or plant by any method whatever; (pêche)
@ref Reg 2(2) "fishing" (src:35)
DECLARE `cr1 Thing caught or taken in fishing` IS ONE OF
    `a fish, including shellfish, crustaceans or molluscs`
    `an aquatic animal or plant`
    `something else that is not a fish or an aquatic animal or plant`

-- fishing means fishing for or catching any fish ... or any aquatic animal or plant by any method whatever.
-- The method is irrelevant ("by any method whatever"), so no input asks for it.
@ref Reg 2(2) "fishing" (src:35)
GIVEN `fishing for or catching` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `cr1 Thing caught or taken in fishing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — an activity is fishing` `fishing for or catching` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `something else that is not a fish or an aquatic animal or plant` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `fishing for or catching`

-- src:45 | hunting means hunting for or catching or killing any wild animal by any method whatever, but does not include any operation involved in carrying on the business of rodent extermination; (chasse)
@ref Reg 2(2) "hunting" (src:45)
GIVEN `hunting for or catching or killing a wild animal by any method` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an operation involved in carrying on the business of rodent extermination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — an activity is hunting` `hunting for or catching or killing a wild animal by any method` `an operation involved in carrying on the business of rodent extermination` MEANS
    `hunting for or catching or killing a wild animal by any method`
    AND (NOT `an operation involved in carrying on the business of rodent extermination`)

-- src:51 | trapping means the operations involved in using any trap, snare or other device for taking or destroying any wild animal, but does not include any operation involved in carrying on the business of rodent extermination. (piégeage)
@ref Reg 2(2) "trapping" (src:51)
GIVEN `using a trap, snare or other device for taking or destroying a wild animal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an operation involved in carrying on the business of rodent extermination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — an activity is trapping` `using a trap, snare or other device for taking or destroying a wild animal` `an operation involved in carrying on the business of rodent extermination` MEANS
    `using a trap, snare or other device for taking or destroying a wild animal`
    AND (NOT `an operation involved in carrying on the business of rodent extermination`)

§§ `Regulation 2(2): forestry, logging and lumbering, and regulation 2(3): timber`

-- Forestry, logging and lumbering are each "when carried on in a forest, on a woodlot or on a tree farm".
-- src:36 | forestry means the planting, breeding, propagation, production, protection, measuring or harvesting of trees when carried on in a forest, on a woodlot or on a tree farm, and includes all services incidental to any of those activities if such services are performed where the activities are carried on; (sylviculture)
@ref Reg 2(2) "forestry", "logging", "lumbering" (src:36)
DECLARE `cr1 Place of forestry work` IS ONE OF
    `in a forest`
    `on a woodlot`
    `on a tree farm`
    `at another place`

-- src:36 | forestry means the planting, breeding, propagation, production, protection, measuring or harvesting of trees when carried on in a forest, on a woodlot or on a tree farm, and includes all services incidental to any of those activities if such services are performed where the activities are carried on; (sylviculture)
@ref Reg 2(2) "forestry" (src:36)
DECLARE `cr1 Operation in the definition of forestry` IS ONE OF
    `planting trees`
    `breeding trees`
    `propagating trees`
    `producing trees`
    `protecting trees`
    `measuring trees`
    `harvesting trees`
    `a service incidental to those activities`
    `another operation on trees`

@ref Reg 2(2) "forestry", "logging", "lumbering" (src:36)
GIVEN place IS A `cr1 Place of forestry work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — a place is a forest, a woodlot or a tree farm` place MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `at another place` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- forestry means the planting, breeding, propagation, production, protection, measuring or harvesting of
-- trees when carried on in a forest, on a woodlot or on a tree farm, and includes all services incidental
-- to any of those activities if the services are performed where the activities are carried on.
@ref Reg 2(2) "forestry" (src:36)
GIVEN operation IS A `cr1 Operation in the definition of forestry`
      place IS A `cr1 Place of forestry work`
      `the service is performed where the activities are carried on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — an operation is forestry` operation place `the service is performed where the activities are carried on` MEANS
    CONSIDER operation
    WHEN `a service incidental to those activities` THEN `the service is performed where the activities are carried on`
    WHEN `another operation on trees` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `reg 2(2) — a place is a forest, a woodlot or a tree farm` place

-- src:52 | (3) For the purposes of the definitions logging and lumbering in subsection (2), timber means logs of any size, lathwood, pulpwood, fuelwood, tiewood, veneerwood, posts, bolts, piles, pit props, spars, stakes, bark, chips or any crude wood before it has been milled or otherwise manufactured.
@ref Reg 2(3) "timber" (src:52)
DECLARE `cr1 Form of wood` IS ONE OF
    `logs of any size`
    `lathwood`
    `pulpwood`
    `fuelwood`
    `tiewood`
    `veneerwood`
    `posts`
    `bolts`
    `piles`
    `pit props`
    `spars`
    `stakes`
    `bark`
    `chips`
    `other crude wood`
    `wood that is not one of those`

-- timber means the forms listed, or any crude wood before it has been milled or otherwise manufactured.
-- The listed forms are timber as listed; "other crude wood" is timber only before it has been milled or
-- otherwise manufactured.
@ref Reg 2(3) "timber" (src:52)
GIVEN form IS A `cr1 Form of wood`
      `it has been milled or otherwise manufactured` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(3) — wood is timber` form `it has been milled or otherwise manufactured` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `other crude wood` THEN NOT `it has been milled or otherwise manufactured`
    WHEN `wood that is not one of those` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- logging means the converting of trees into timber when carried on in a forest, on a woodlot or on a tree
-- farm; "timber" is the regulation 2(3) word, so the product of the conversion is tested with it.
-- src:49 | logging means the converting of trees into timber when carried on in a forest, on a woodlot or on a tree farm; (exploitation forestière)
@ref Reg 2(2) "logging" (src:49)
GIVEN `converting trees into the wood` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wood produced` IS A `cr1 Form of wood`
      `the wood produced has been milled or otherwise manufactured` IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `cr1 Place of forestry work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — an activity is logging` `converting trees into the wood` `the wood produced` `the wood produced has been milled or otherwise manufactured` place MEANS
        `converting trees into the wood`
    AND `reg 2(3) — wood is timber` `the wood produced` `the wood produced has been milled or otherwise manufactured`
    AND `reg 2(2) — a place is a forest, a woodlot or a tree farm` place

-- lumbering means the milling of timber into lumber or boards when carried on in a forest, on a woodlot or
-- on a tree farm, and includes the preparation of timber for milling in such place. The timber milled, or
-- prepared for milling, is by the nature of the act wood that has not yet been milled.
-- src:50 | lumbering means the milling of timber into lumber or boards when carried on in a forest, on a woodlot or on a tree farm, and includes the preparation of timber for milling in such place; (débit des bois)
@ref Reg 2(2) "lumbering" (src:50)
GIVEN `milling timber into lumber or boards, or preparing timber for milling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wood milled or prepared` IS A `cr1 Form of wood`
      place IS A `cr1 Place of forestry work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — an activity is lumbering` `milling timber into lumber or boards, or preparing timber for milling` `the wood milled or prepared` place MEANS
        `milling timber into lumber or boards, or preparing timber for milling`
    AND `reg 2(3) — wood is timber` `the wood milled or prepared` FALSE
    AND `reg 2(2) — a place is a forest, a woodlot or a tree farm` place

§§ `Regulation 2(2): horticulture and international organization`

-- src:37 | horticulture means
-- src:38 | (a) the operations relating to the breeding, producing, raising or harvesting of
-- src:39 | (i) vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses, and
-- src:40 | (ii) seeds, seedlings, grafts and cuttings of vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses, and
-- src:41 | (b) the operations relating to landscape gardening where the landscape gardening is incidental to the carrying on of
-- src:42 | (i) any of the operations described in paragraph (a), or
-- src:43 | (ii) agriculture,
-- src:44 | and includes all services incidental to the carrying on of any of the operations described in paragraph (a) or (b) if such services are performed where the operations are carried on; (horticulture)
@ref Reg 2(2) "horticulture" (src:37-44)
DECLARE `cr1 Operation in the definition of horticulture` IS ONE OF
    `breeding, producing, raising or harvesting vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses`
    `breeding, producing, raising or harvesting seeds, seedlings, grafts or cuttings of vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses`
    `landscape gardening`
    `a service incidental to those operations`
    `another operation in gardening`

-- horticulture means (a) the breeding, producing, raising or harvesting operations of (i) and (ii), and
-- (b) landscape gardening where it is incidental to paragraph (a) or to agriculture, and includes all
-- services incidental to (a) or (b) if they are performed where the operations are carried on.
@ref Reg 2(2) "horticulture" (src:37-44)
GIVEN operation IS A `cr1 Operation in the definition of horticulture`
      `landscape gardening is incidental to those operations or to agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is performed where the operations are carried on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — an operation is horticulture` operation `landscape gardening is incidental to those operations or to agriculture` `the service is performed where the operations are carried on` MEANS
    CONSIDER operation
    WHEN `landscape gardening` THEN `landscape gardening is incidental to those operations or to agriculture`
    WHEN `a service incidental to those operations` THEN `the service is performed where the operations are carried on`
    WHEN `another operation in gardening` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:46 | international organization means
-- src:47 | (a) any specialized agency of which Canada is a member that is brought into relationship with the United Nations in accordance with Article 63 of the Charter of the United Nations, and
-- src:48 | (b) any international organization of which Canada is a member, the primary purpose of which is the maintenance of international peace or the economic or social well-being of a community of nations; (organisation internationale)
@ref Reg 2(2) "international organization" (src:46-48)
GIVEN `a specialized agency of which Canada is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `brought into relationship with the United Nations in accordance with Article 63 of the Charter of the United Nations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an international organization of which Canada is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its primary purpose is the maintenance of international peace or the economic or social well-being of a community of nations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2(2) — a body is an international organization` `a specialized agency of which Canada is a member` `brought into relationship with the United Nations in accordance with Article 63 of the Charter of the United Nations` `an international organization of which Canada is a member` `its primary purpose is the maintenance of international peace or the economic or social well-being of a community of nations` MEANS
        (`a specialized agency of which Canada is a member`
         AND `brought into relationship with the United Nations in accordance with Article 63 of the Charter of the United Nations`)
    OR  (`an international organization of which Canada is a member`
         AND `its primary purpose is the maintenance of international peace or the economic or social well-being of a community of nations`)
